When writing an integration test in `consensus/core/tests/`, I can only import items that are `pub` in `consensus/core/src/lib.rs`. If I need access to internal modules like `block`, `context`, `dag_state`, etc., I must either:
1. Use the public re-exports if available (e.g., `consensus_core::BlockAPI` instead of `consensus_core::block::BlockAPI`).
2. If the test requires internal access, it MUST be an internal test (inside `src/` and registered in `lib.rs`).
3. Since I cannot modify `lib.rs` to register a new internal test module, I am stuck unless I can find an existing internal test file to append to, or if the public API is sufficient.

Checking `lib.rs` again, `dag_state` is re-exported as `pub use dag_state::DagState;`. `BlockAPI` is re-exported. `TestBlock`, `Transaction`, `VerifiedBlock` are re-exported. `Context` is re-exported. `MemStore` is re-exported. `DagBuilder` is re-exported. `UniversalCommitter` is NOT re-exported. `LeaderSchedule` is NOT re-exported.

So I can write an integration test using `DagState`, `DagBuilder`, `MemStore`, `Context`, `VerifiedBlock`. But I cannot use `UniversalCommitter` or `LeaderSchedule` directly if they are not public.

